## Program Outcome

The hosted dashboard exposes privacy-bounded per-instance reporter and release health, identifies
divergent installations without inventing consensus, and makes every project summary's source and
freshness visible while remaining advisory and read-only.

## M1-REPORTER-AND-RELEASE-TRUTH — Extend the bounded contract

Status: active
Depends on: none

Outcome: Report and persist the smallest controlled set of per-instance health, semantic digest,
and release-provenance facts already known by the local instance.

Gates:

- `G1-REPORTER-HEALTH-CONTRACT`: strict allowlisting, bounded codes and counts, explicit heartbeat,
  delivery, and quiescence semantics, and no paths, logs, scheduler definitions, credentials, raw
  diagnostics, or arbitrary text.
- `G2-RELEASE-PROVENANCE`: installed, stable, candidate/pending, and production-verified release
  states name their controlled source, observation time, and unknown behavior.

Candidate campaign: `implement-dashboard-release-reporter-and-instance-health`.

## M2-INSTANCE-HEALTH-WORK2 — Present and qualify fleet trust

Status: active
Depends on: M1

Outcome: Show a compact readable project trust summary and per-instance health table that preserves
independent source truth and highlights deterministic semantic divergence.

Gate:

- `G3-INSTANCE-DIVERGENCE-UI`: release posture, freshness, reporting condition, and divergence are
  visible per instance; project aggregation never merges conflicting lifecycle snapshots; the
  authenticated hosted UI remains advisory, read-only, and live through semantic SSE.

Candidate campaign: `implement-dashboard-release-reporter-and-instance-health`.

